-- title:
--   Toric part lies in finite part of pⁿ-torsion, with bound
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a nonzero natural number $M$ with $p \mid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$ (so $A$ lies over $p$), whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$. Let $\Lambda$ be level data at $A$ for $(p,M,H)$: a structure morphism $\sigma_A \colon \operatorname{Spec} A \to \operatorname{Spec} \mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ (where $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ is the subring `ratLocalizedAt p` of rationals with denominator coprime to $p$) compatible with the generic point, a scheme $\Lambda.X$ over $\operatorname{Spec} \mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ with a relative group law $\Lambda.L$, and bijections identifying $J_{H'}(M/p) = \mathrm{Pic}^0$ of `xHFunctionFieldBar (M / p) (infSubgroup p M H hpM)` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, where $H'$ is the image of $H$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^{\times}$, with the generic sections of $\Lambda.f$, and $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the residue-field function field with the sections over the special point. Let $O$ be a `JHNeronObjectAtP` over $\Lambda$, so in particular a smooth, separated, quasi-compact, surjective, locally of finite type morphism $g$ with commutative relative group law $L$, a Hecke-equivariant, Galois-equivariant additive bijection $\mathrm{pts} \colon J_H(M) \to$ sections of $g$ over the generic point, and the further data of $O$. Assume $\Lambda.f$ is an abelian scheme in the sense of the bundle `AbelianSchemePropertyBundle` (smooth, proper, connected fibres, and admitting a relative group law), and that $\Lambda.\mathrm{pts}$ is additive for $\Lambda.L$. Then, for every $n$, writing $m = p^n$: the subgroup $O.\mathrm{toricPts}(m)$ of $J_H(M)$ generated by the toric points $O.\mathrm{toricPoint}\,m$ (indexed by the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-valued characters of `muCoord A O.toricRank m`) is contained in $O.\mathrm{finPts}(m)$, the subgroup generated by those $m$-torsion classes $x$ in $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` whose point $O.\mathrm{pts}(x)$ factors through an $A$-valued point over $\sigma_A$; moreover $O.\mathrm{finPts}(m)$ is finite, the $m$-torsion subgroup of $J_{H'}(M/p)$ is finite, and $$\#\,O.\mathrm{finPts}(p^n) \le \#\,O.\mathrm{toricPts}(p^n) \cdot \bigl(\#\,J_{H'}(M/p)[p^n]\bigr)^{2}.$$
--
--   This is the upper-bound half of the computation of the order of the finite part of the $p^n$-torsion on the Néron model of $J_H(M)$ at a prime $p$ exactly dividing the level, the toric part being the contribution of the split torus in the special fibre and the factor $(\#J_{H'}(M/p)[p^n])^2$ the contribution of the two copies of the lower-level Jacobian. It is used in the construction separating the old lattice from the toric lattice inside the Tate module of $J_H(M)$, the input to level lowering at $p$.
